{
	"note": "Files other than shell32.dll that an icon patcher rewrites, each guarded by the SHA-256 of the stock 0.4.16 i386 file. Which groups of a file are replaced comes from Afterglow's map.json: every group it verifies for that module. A `groups` list on a file adds only groups the map does not name, each with its icon. See docs/icon-survey.md. The `map-icons` family holds the remaining modules the map names, including the ones the `base` trim removes; a patcher leaves a trimmed file alone (RL-53.3). `explorer.exe` and its copy `agexplorer.exe` list group 100 (the program's own icon, the first group in the file, which Explorer's file views draw) because the map names only group 101 (the Start menu entry) for `explorer`. A file with `new_file` has no stock file: the patcher creates it as a resource-only DLL holding the groups the map names for it (`imageres.dll`, which only the Show Desktop button loads), and refuses when the stock disk already has one. The colours Afterglow's map records as compiled into code (`colours`: the felt of `sol.exe` and `spider.exe`) are written into the file of the module that holds them, over the exact bytes the map names, after the stock file's SHA-256 is checked.",
